<Docs title="Store a secret — Botpasses" crumbs={[{ href: "/docs", label: "Docs" }, { href: "/docs/how-to/store-a-secret", label: "Store a secret" }]}>
  <h1>Store a secret</h1>
  <p>Sign in, open the <a href="/console">console</a>, and store a named item. Allowed hosts must match the API the agent will call (for example <code>api.spotify.com</code>).</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <a href="/sign-up">Create account</a>, confirm the email code, enroll TOTP.</li>
    <li>In the console Vault, choose <strong>Store credential</strong>. Name is env-var style: <code>SPOTIFY_SECRET</code>. Kind <strong>API token</strong> sends <code>Authorization: Bearer</code>. Kind <strong>Client ID and secret</strong> is a Spotify app secret (Client ID + Client Secret). It is stored as <code>client_secret</code>, not a token. Use <em>Change how it is sent</em> only for HTTP Basic or a raw header. Edit on the vault row reuses this form; leave Value blank to keep the current secret. Rotate is the value-only shortcut. On <code>staging.botpasses.com</code> the environment is staging only. If Store is rejected, the dialog stays open and shows the API error. The value field is not cleared.</li>
    <li>Set allowed hosts to the HTTPS hostname only. Not a full URL.</li>
    <li>If an agent already asked, open Inbox and choose <strong>Store the credential</strong>, or open the <code>collect_url</code> it returned. Type the value on this origin. Never paste it into chat.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Local sqlite (no hosted account):</p>
  <pre><code>printf '%s' 'sk_test_example_not_real' | npx vault set STRIPE_KEY</code></pre>
  <p>API: <a href="/docs/reference/http-api">POST /api/items</a>. MCP miss: <a href="/docs/reference/mcp-tools">need_item + collect_url</a>.</p>
</Docs>
